{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1513151-vestige-creation-help","id":1513151,"title":"Vestige creation help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-28T19:52:47-07:00","id":1513151,"title":"Vestige creation help","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> I love the vestige descriptions and detailed text in the core book, but I am not really imaginative enough to see all <b>Virtue </b>/ <b>Vice </b>combination working? I was wondering how would a <b>Trustworthy </b>/ <b>Treacherous </b>vestige have a resonant memory. Or a <b>Trustworthy </b>/ <b>Lazy</b>.<br /> <br /> Can the forumites help with the example?<br /> <br /> Lets say a level 6 vestige (sorcerer made).<br /> <br /> Thanks,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 05-28-2023, 11:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T20:44:06-07:00","id":1513157,"title":"","content":"A vestige's Virtue and Vice are both expressions of the emotion that created the memory that empowers it. Contradictory combinations are obviously going to run into trouble and the solution is generally to not use them in your designs unless you actually have an idea of how to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T15:19:53-07:00","id":1513331,"title":"","content":"The Virtue/Vice list is not exhaustive, (so we can add more whenever), but I agree contradictory combinations are tricky.<br /> That said we can assume something that makes it a lot easier to work with in your chosen example.<br /> <br /> 6 dot Vestiges are created intentionally. As such, we only need a single instance. (&quot;Natural&quot; Vestiges probably require more consistency with the emotions involved.)<br /> <br /> So for Trustworthy/Treacherous we can assume that either sorcerer was casting a wide net of people who can use it, or that they had mixed feelings about the memory in question. For example, they were called on to deal with a matter between two of their allies and the divided loyalties messed with the sorcerer's head. They proved they were Trustworthy to one ally, by betraying another.<br /> <br /> Trustworthy/Lazy is a far easier combination, as one can keep confidence and be consistent with their support, while still dragging their feet or trying to avoid significant effort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T19:27:22-07:00","id":1513495,"title":"","content":"Trustworthy/treacherous sounds to me like someone was offered a prisoners dilemma and had to make a choice where their life depended on if they could depend on someone else or to betray them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}